course: dictionary
lesson: 15736
title: Transmit: sending and passing on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Transmit» is a word with three main meanings, and context tells you which one you need. «The radio station transmits its music across the whole city.» Here, transmit means sending out signals, so the music travels through the air to people's radios.
explain: «Mosquitoes can transmit illness when they bite people.» The clue is the word illness. Transmit here means passing something, such as an illness, from one person or thing to another. The bite is how the illness moves from one to the next.
explain: «Clean glass transmits light, so you can see right through it.» Transmit can also mean letting light, heat, sound or electricity pass through. To check your meaning, swap in «lets through» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Transmit» means to send something out, or to pass something on.
fact: «Transmit» can mean sending radio, TV or electronic signals.
fact: «Transmit» can mean passing a disease from one person or thing to another.
fact: «Transmit» can mean letting light, heat, sound or electricity pass through, as in «Glass transmits light.»
fact: The forms transmit, transmits, transmitted and transmitting all come from the same word.
exercise: «The radio station transmits its music across the city.» What does transmit mean here? | To paint a picture | To stop something from moving | To hide something under the ground | *To send out signals
exercise: Which of these is a way an illness can be transmitted? | *A cough or a bite from someone who is ill | Drawing a map | Singing a song | Reading a book
exercise: «Glass transmits light.» What does transmits mean in this sentence? | Makes light change colour | Turns light into sound | *Lets light pass through | Blocks light completely
test: «Copper wire transmits electricity well.» What does transmits mean here? | Ignores electricity completely | Makes electricity from the sun | Stores electricity in a box | *Lets electricity pass through
test: Which word could replace transmitted in «The cold was transmitted from Sam to his sister.»? | Hidden | *Passed on | Caught | Forgotten
exam: «Metals transmit heat and electricity well.» What does transmit mean? | *Pass through | Ignore | Freeze | Store
